Z||000009||Alex4mula||08-07-2000||11:28 AM||||I received this e-mail saying that if you pay over the ticketed amount at least you don't get the points. They way it works is that they send you a check for the amount over and you do NOT cash it. Their check will not clear and apparently they cannot assess points on outstanding accounts (computer system). Haven't tried but sounds possible...||||reg||1
Z||000010||Fret Naught||08-09-2000||12:48 PM||||I guess I am pretty lucky or calm one of the two, I haven't been pulled over since I sold the Harley, Seems they liked to pull over Harley riders for any reason, some of the excuses, You didn't put your feet down at the stop sign. You got to close to the white line, you got to close to the yellow line, you kept ducking your head it looked suspicious (dodging bugs) your tail light isn't bright enough. your turn signal isn't flashing. I never once got pulled over for speeding or anything important, just nonsense stuff. I got tired of it and sold the bike about 3 years ago. I guess they won.||||reg||12
Z||000011||blayde8||08-09-2000||03:47 PM||||School license?? You're lucky.  I am 15 and we don't have such a thing like that in Minnesota.  Sorry about that ticket, it shouldn't have happened.  I can't wait until I get my license to. <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/cool.gif">||||reg||1
